From fdbf763b921e2b184daf341612154453d5bf8bb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:59:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: notify ubus when a link reconfiguration changes a
 station's links

A Link Reconfiguration adds or removes affiliated links of an associated
non-AP MLD without a new association, so no sta-authorized names the
new set, and a ubus subscriber that reports the links of a client MLD
keeps the old ones.

The change takes effect at the TX status of the Link Reconfiguration
Response: an added link is undone there where the response was not
acknowledged, and a removed link is freed there. Once the response is
acknowledged and it accepted a link, send sta-links-changed for the
association link's station, which holds the links after a removal moved
the association link. The event carries the same station fields as
sta-authorized: ap_mld_address, assoc_link_id and links.

This depends on 197-ap-mld-drop-a-link-that-goes-from-the-station-links:
without it, an added link that was undone stays valid on the station,
and the next sta-links-changed names it. The two land together.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -1663,9 +1663,6 @@ void hostapd_link_reconf_resp_tx_status(
 		goto exit;
 	}
 
-	if (dl_list_empty(&req_list->del_req))
-		goto exit;
-
 	dl_list_for_each(info, &req_list->del_req, struct link_reconf_req_info,
 			 list) {
 		if (info->status != WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
@@ -1751,6 +1748,9 @@ void hostapd_link_reconf_resp_tx_status(
 		ap_free_link_sta(lhapd, lsta);
 	}
 
+	if (req_list->links_add_ok || req_list->links_del_ok)
+		hostapd_ubus_notify_sta_links(assoc_hapd, assoc_sta);
+
 exit:
 	ml_deinit_link_reconf_req(&req_list);
 	if (assoc_sta && assoc_sta->reconf_req)
